WEBVTT

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:37.300
Fallout, an increasingly important word in the atomic and hydrogen age,

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:44.850
a word that often causes questions, uneasy speculation about what it is and what we can do about it.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:52.640
The facts from federal civil defense tell us that fallout could hurt you, might even kill you.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:59.270
But that knowledge of a few simple rules and definite precautions might save your life.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.940
You, of course, are more than one person.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:08.410
You're an entire family, made up of all the people who are puzzled by Fallout,

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.220
but who will be able to cope with it effectively when you know what to do.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.220
But initially, your puzzle concern is understandable,

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:25.300
because Fallout seems mysterious, although actually it is not.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.200
But it is true that you can't taste it.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:41.860
you can't hear it, can't smell it, can't feel it. Often you can't even see it. So it's no wonder

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:49.450
you're a bit perplexed. Ready to ask civil defense? Well, what about it, mister? What

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:58.880
is this fallout stuff? The answer is simply this. When an enemy A-bomb or an H-bomb explodes,

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:12.910
Close to the ground, thousands of tons of earth and debris would be sucked upward, sometimes to 80,000 feet or more.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.120
They help form the mushroom cloud.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:24.500
Fallout is nothing more than particles of matter in the air made radioactive by nuclear explosion.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.970
The larger radioactive particles spill out in...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.500
the immediate area of the explosion right away but others although you may not see them may be

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:49.970
carried by the upper winds for many miles sooner or later however they settle to earth this is

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:58.700
fallout and it can be very dangerous if you don't know what to do about it well do you know what to

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.540
do about it, Grandpa.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:06.370
not yet young man but i will what i'd like to know is what's the relationship of this fallout to the

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:13.300
other aspects of an atomic explosion okay grandpa to get that answer let's go back to the explosion

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:26.250
there are four major characteristics of an a-bomb or h-bomb explosion they are blast heat initial

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.980
radiation and residual radiation.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.750
The last of these, residual radiation, is given off by the fallout from the explosion.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:45.700
The first three occur almost simultaneously, depending on how far you are from the point of explosion.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:55.190
Your chief protection from these would be the distance you are from the center of the explosion, plus adequate shelter.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:59.940
But radioactive fallout will fall.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.200
back to Earth over a much larger area.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:04.380
than that affected by heat.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:05.270
Blast.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.520
and initial radiation.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.240
The Radioactive Cloud.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:12.570
would spread mostly downwind from the explosion.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.290
winds at all altitudes,

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.820
particularly those in the upper atmosphere,

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.000
would carry the fallout over a large area.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:29.670
The size of the area and the distance would depend on the size of the bomb.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.380
and the speed and direction of the wind.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:38.620
Fallout in dangerous concentrations can be carried by the winds,

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.860
or 200 miles or more.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.000
This is important to remember, son.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.410
because most of us live within...

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:49.810
two hundred miles of a city

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.490
whose destruction might be important to an enemy.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:59.520
And while fallout loses some of its radioactivity before it eventually reaches the ground,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.080
it's still dangerous to you and your family.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:04.880
even for days.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.690
weeks or longer

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.060
after the explosion.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.160
It's a threat not only to humans,

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.520
but also to animals and crops.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.920
and to the people who depend on them.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.810
it can contaminate your home

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:20.810
car.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:21.570
Yard.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:22.920
and water supply.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.810
normally these could not be used

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.400
until the radiation had decayed to an acceptable level.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.040
or they had been decontaminated.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.690
All this clear so far, sister?

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.080
Sure, but you've talked about fallout from enemy bombing.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:44.670
Now, how about fallout from our own testing of atomic weapons in Nevada

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.270
that I read about in the newspaper?

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:52.360
Our government very carefully tests only small nuclear devices in the United States.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:57.410
These tests are not conducted unless weather conditions are favorable,

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.960
and there will be no danger.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.940
to animals.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:01.960
crops,

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:02.700
property

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:03.600
industry

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:04.500
or people.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.310
The scientists check weather conditions carefully.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:15.870
to assure that the small amounts of fallout carried by the winds travel only over open country.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.050
away from people.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.520
Well, I'm still worried about people.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:21.850
My people.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:22.930
My family.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.810
How do we protect ourselves from fallout from enemy bombing?

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:29.940
There is defense against radio.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.900
active fallout.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:32.220
Shelter.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:36.660
Almost any kind of cover will afford some protection.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:41.560
Just getting indoors can cut the radiation hazard in half.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:43.800
in an alert.

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:47.910
civil defense officials will tell you what to do to protect yourselves

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.840
prediction of the fallout area

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.650
will be made by civil defense.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:01.640
and Weather Bureau personnel.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:06.820
so that people in those areas where fallout might occur

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.070
can be given advance warning.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.580
Outside the actual bomb zone,

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:17.630
Your survival chances against dangerous fallout are excellent.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.600
If you take suitable

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:20.820
Shelter.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:26.460
One of your best protections is an outdoor underground shelter.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.200
covered with at least three feet of earth.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:33.560
The Earth will cut the radiation rate inside.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.060
to approximately one five thousandth of the rate of off-ground.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.400
It's important to get undercover.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:43.400
fast.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:47.420
Maybe a day or even a week before it's safe to come out.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.000
except for short periods.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.250
depending on the radiation level.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:53.980
Another good bet.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.460
is a basement shelter.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.940
where the radiation level would be one-tenth or even less of that.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:00.520
outside.

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:06.210
Your shelter would meet the specifications recommended in the FCDA publications.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:13.770
If you don't have a prepared shelter, your basement alone will offer considerable protection.

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:21.070
And if your house has no basement, close the windows and stay on the first floor.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:29.480
In an ordinary frame house, the fallout radiation level would be only about one half of what

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:29.900
it would be

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:38.080
outdoors in a brick or stone house it would be even less but if you're caught

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:43.920
in open country almost any kind of cover will give you some protection against

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:52.740
the worst effects of fallout get into a barn a car under trees anything and stay

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:59.780
there until you get word to come out in a pinch dig a foxhole make a cover of

00:08:59.780 --> 00:08:59.960
brand

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:09.200
or board. Don't let radioactive dust touch your skin. Of course, you can't stock a foxhole,

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:17.930
but you can stock your prepared shelter in advance with a seven-day supply of food, water,

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:26.090
two gallons for each person, and an extra gallon for junior, blankets, first-aid kit,

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:29.000
flashlight with extra batteries.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:36.790
and a battery-operated radio, so you can receive civil defense instructions as to when it's safe to come out.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:44.580
Remember, dangerous radioactive fallout is like dust and can be removed like dust.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:52.620
Leave your badly contaminated clothing outside until radiation decays before washing them.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:58.240
Wash with soap and water. Take a shower if possible.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.910
Uncovered food or water, which might have been contaminated, should not be used.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.130
Wash unopened containers before opening.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.200
The food will be safe.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:15.740
Perhaps you can sweep roofs or flush them with a hose,

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:20.650
but only after you've been instructed by your Civil Defense Radiological Monitor.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:26.280
So these are the facts that should reassure and encourage you.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.940
Encourage families all over America.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:33.840
And the facts mostly hinge on effective use of shelters.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:42.030
Learn about shelters and other means by which you can protect yourself and your family from radioactive fallout.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:45.900
Available at your local civil defense headquarters.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:52.980
Be ready to assist in defense preparations in your community if your help is needed.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:59.980
For fallout is only one of the problems which the nation must be prepared to meet if it is to...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.440
to survive in the nuclear age.
